{
  "version": "basic-seasonings-v2",
  "source": "Owner decision of 2026-10-29 (widens basic-seasonings-v1, which was operations/sprint2-plan/08-household.md section 3.2; ADR-0068; ADR-0072 section 2): the thirteen basics plus rice, vinegars, small-amount sauces and condiments, spices, dried herbs, stock cubes, starches and flours. Every id is a normalized name in data-engineering/data/release/v2.2/ingredients.jsonl.",
  "rule": "An ingredient listed here is assumed at home only for shopping, pricing and the budget: it is left off the list and unpriced unless the household lists it in missing_basics. It stays a recipe ingredient for every safety check (allergens, exclusions, diets), and one the household excludes is never assumed. Cooking sauces and pastes that are a dish's base (marinara, curry paste, pesto, salsa), tomato products, coconut milk, honey, peanut butter, jam, olive oil, butter, liquid broths, baking items, breadcrumbs, pasta, noodles and fresh herbs are bought. Allergens are the runtime vocabulary's, mapped from the release's (release molluscs read as shellfish, gluten_candidate as gluten, sulfites unchecked).",
